## 1. Purpose & Problem Statement

The Hospital Management System digitizes hospital operations currently run on paper, which causes: lost/misplaced patient records, long registration queues, scheduling conflicts, poor staff coordination, and inaccessible patient history. The system centralizes patient management, appointment scheduling, and electronic medical records (EMR) behind role-based access control.

## 2. Objectives

1. Digitize patient registration and record-keeping.
2. Allow patients to book and track appointments.
3. Give doctors and authorized staff controlled access to patient data and history.
4. Enable electronic medical record creation and management.
5. Provide role-specific dashboards.
6. Enforce data security and role-based access at every layer.

## 3. Scope

### In scope (v1 / MVP)
Authentication & roles, patient registration/management, appointment scheduling, EMR core functions, five role dashboards, role-restricted search.

### Out of scope (v1 — see §12 for full list)
Pharmacy, billing/insurance, SMS/email notifications, audit logs, multi-branch support, file uploads.

## 4. Actors

| Actor | Summary |
|---|---|
| Administrator | Manages users, roles, staff, and oversees hospital-wide activity |
| Doctor | Views assigned patients, manages EMR, views appointments |
| Nurse | Views/updates authorized patient data; cannot diagnose or finalize records |
| Receptionist | Registers patients, manages appointments; no clinical data access |
| Patient | Manages own profile, books appointments, views own permitted records |

