## 5. Functional Requirements

Each requirement has an ID, description, actor(s), acceptance criteria, and MoSCoW priority. **Must** = MVP/Sprint 1–2. **Should** = Sprint 3–4. **Could** = stretch if time allows. **Won't** (this version) = deferred, see §12.

### 5.1 Authentication & Authorization

| ID | Requirement | Actor(s) | Acceptance Criteria | Priority |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| FR-1.1 | User logs in with email/username and password | All | Valid credentials return a JWT; invalid credentials return 401 with no detail on which field was wrong | Must |
| FR-1.2 | User logs out, invalidating the active session token client-side | All | Token removed from client storage; subsequent API calls with the old token still work until expiry (stateless JWT — document this limitation) | Must |
| FR-1.3 | System enforces role-based authorization on every protected endpoint | All | A request to an endpoint outside the caller's role returns 403, not 500 or silent success | Must |
| FR-1.4 | Administrator creates staff accounts and assigns roles | Admin | New account cannot log in until a role is assigned; attempting to assign an invalid role is rejected | Must |
| FR-1.5 | Patient self-registers an account | Patient | Duplicate email is rejected; password meets minimum complexity rules (defined by Security, §7) | Should |

### 5.2 Patient Management

| ID | Requirement | Actor(s) | Acceptance Criteria | Priority |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| FR-2.1 | Receptionist/Admin registers a new patient | Receptionist, Admin | Required fields (name, DOB, phone, emergency contact) enforced; duplicate-patient check runs on name+DOB before save | Must |
| FR-2.2 | Authorized user views a patient's demographic profile | Receptionist, Doctor, Nurse, Admin | Clinical fields (diagnosis, EMR) are NOT returned to Receptionist's view — see FR-7.2 | Must |
| FR-2.3 | Authorized user updates patient demographic info | Receptionist, Admin | Edits are validated (e.g., phone format); update timestamp recorded | Must |
| FR-2.4 | Authorized user searches patients by name/ID/phone | Receptionist, Doctor, Nurse, Admin | Search results are filtered server-side by the caller's role before being returned — never filtered only in the UI | Must |
| FR-2.5 | Patient views and edits own permitted profile fields | Patient | Patient cannot edit DOB or Patient ID once set | Should |

### 5.3 Appointment Management

| ID | Requirement | Actor(s) | Acceptance Criteria | Priority |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| FR-3.1 | Receptionist creates an appointment (patient, doctor, date, time, reason) | Receptionist | System rejects a slot already booked for that doctor at that date/time | Must |
| FR-3.2 | Patient requests an appointment | Patient | Created in "Pending" status; cannot self-confirm | Should |
| FR-3.3 | Doctor views own scheduled appointments | Doctor | Only appointments where `DoctorId` = caller's ID are returned | Must |
| FR-3.4 | Receptionist/Admin updates appointment status (Pending → Confirmed → Completed/Cancelled) | Receptionist, Admin | Invalid transitions (e.g., Completed → Pending) are rejected | Must |
| FR-3.5 | Patient views own appointment status | Patient | Only the requesting patient's own appointments are returned | Must |

### 5.4 Electronic Medical Records (EMR)

| ID | Requirement | Actor(s) | Acceptance Criteria | Priority |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| FR-4.1 | Doctor creates a medical record (symptoms, diagnosis, treatment, prescription, notes) tied to a patient and appointment | Doctor | Record cannot be created without a valid PatientId; record is timestamped and attributed to the authoring doctor | Must |
| FR-4.2 | Doctor updates own-authored medical record | Doctor | A doctor cannot edit a record authored by a different doctor | Should |
| FR-4.3 | Doctor/authorized staff views a patient's medical history | Doctor | Full history returned only to Doctor and Admin; Nurse sees a restricted subset (§7) | Must |
| FR-4.4 | Nurse adds vitals to a patient record without editing diagnosis | Nurse | Nurse's write access is scoped to a `Vitals` sub-entity only — enforced server-side | Should |
| FR-4.5 | Patient views own permitted medical record summary | Patient | Patient sees diagnosis/treatment summary; does NOT see doctor's internal notes field | Could |

### 5.5 Dashboards

| ID | Requirement | Actor(s) | Acceptance Criteria | Priority |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| FR-5.1 | Each role sees a dashboard scoped to their permitted data (Admin: system overview; Doctor: appointments + patients; Nurse: assigned patients; Receptionist: registration + scheduling; Patient: profile + appointments) | All | Logging in as Role X never renders a UI element whose underlying API call Role X is not authorized to make | Must |

### 5.6 Search

| ID | Requirement | Actor(s) | Acceptance Criteria | Priority |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| FR-6.1 | Role-appropriate search across patients, appointments, staff | Per role | See FR-2.4 — authorization enforced server-side, not just hidden in UI | Must |

