## 6. Data Model

| Entity | Key Fields | Relationships |
|---|---|---|
| **User** | UserId (PK), Email, PasswordHash, RoleId (FK) | 1 User → 1 Role |
| **Role** | RoleId (PK), RoleName | 1 Role → many Users |
| **Patient** | PatientId (PK), FullName, DOB, Gender, Phone, Email, Address, EmergencyContact | 1 Patient → many Appointments; 1 Patient → many MedicalRecords |
| **Doctor** | DoctorId (PK), UserId (FK), Specialty | 1 Doctor → many Appointments; 1 Doctor → many MedicalRecords (as author) |
| **Appointment** | AppointmentId (PK), PatientId (FK), DoctorId (FK), DateTime, Reason, Status (enum: Pending/Confirmed/Completed/Cancelled) | Many-to-1 with Patient and Doctor |
| **MedicalRecord** | RecordId (PK), PatientId (FK), DoctorId (FK, author), AppointmentId (FK, nullable), Date, Symptoms, Diagnosis, Treatment, Prescription, Notes | Many-to-1 with Patient and Doctor; append-only — edits create a new version, not an overwrite (decision needed from DB Manager + Security, flagged open) |
| **Vitals** | VitalId (PK), PatientId (FK), RecordedBy (FK → User), DateTime, BP, Temp, HeartRate | Many-to-1 with Patient; writable by Nurse (FR-4.4) |

**Open decision before Sprint 1:** whether `MedicalRecord` edits are versioned (audit-friendly, more complex) or direct overwrites (simpler, loses history). DB Manager and Security Engineer must agree and document the decision here before EMR tickets are written.

