## 7. Security & Access Control Matrix

| Data / Action | Admin | Doctor | Nurse | Receptionist | Patient |
|---|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|
| Patient demographics (view) | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | Own only |
| Patient demographics (edit) | ✅ | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ | Partial (own, non-ID fields) |
| Diagnosis / treatment (view) | ✅ | ✅ | Restricted summary | ❌ | Own, no notes |
| Diagnosis / treatment (edit) | ❌ | Own-authored only | ❌ | ❌ | ❌ |
| Vitals (write) | ❌ | ✅ | ✅ | ❌ | ❌ |
| Doctor's internal notes | ✅ | Own-authored | ❌ | ❌ | ❌ |
| Appointment create | ✅ | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ | Request only (Pending) |
| Appointment status change | ✅ | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ | ❌ |
| User/role management | ✅ | ❌ | ❌ | ❌ | ❌ |

**Non-negotiable:** every ❌ above must be enforced server-side (API/authorization policy), never only hidden in the frontend UI. QA tests every ❌ cell explicitly (§9).

### Other security requirements
- SEC-1: Passwords hashed via ASP.NET Core Identity defaults; minimum 8 characters, 1 number, 1 special character.
- SEC-2: JWT expiry set to 60 minutes; refresh-token strategy decided before Sprint 2.
- SEC-3: All protected endpoints require a valid role claim; missing/invalid claim → 401, insufficient role → 403.
- SEC-4: API responses never include PasswordHash or other internal-only fields, regardless of caller role.
- SEC-5: Input validation on all write endpoints (server-side, not just client-side forms).

