## 8. Non-Functional Requirements (measurable)

| ID | Requirement |
|---|---|
| NFR-1 (Performance) | 95% of API responses return in under 500ms under normal load (single-instance dev/test environment) |
| NFR-2 (Security) | 100% of protected endpoints tested against unauthorized-role access (see §9) before Sprint close |
| NFR-3 (Usability) | A first-time Receptionist can complete patient registration in under 5 fields of required input without external help |
| NFR-4 (Reliability) | No data loss on concurrent writes to the same Patient record — last-write conflicts must be handled, not silently dropped |
| NFR-5 (Maintainability) | Backend organized by feature module (Controllers/Services per domain: Patients, Appointments, EMR, Auth) so any engineer can locate a feature in under 1 minute |
| NFR-6 (Scalability) | Database schema allows adding a new entity (e.g., Prescription) without breaking existing foreign key relationships |

